    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Fascination! is a 1983 extended play by The Human League, released on Virgin as a stop-gap between Dare and Hysteria. It captures the band at their commercial peak, distilling their sleek synth-pop into a tight, dance-oriented set built around the hit single “(Keep Feeling) Fascination,” along with “Mirror Man,” “Hard Times,” and the previously unreleased “I Love You Too Much.”\n\nMusically, the record leans into polished electronic textures, crisp drum programming, and a more streamlined pop sensibility than the band’s earlier, darker work. It helped extend the success of Dare in the U.S. and Canada, and its inclusion of both hit material and key B-sides made it an effective showcase for The Human League’s evolving sound and mainstream appeal.",
